arXiv:2509.09177v1 [cs.LG] 11 Sep 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Clip Your Sequences Fairly: 
<br class="ltx_break">Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence<span id="id1" class="ltx_text">-</span>Level RL</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Hanyi Mao
</span><span id="id2" class="ltx_note ltx_note_frontmatter ltx_thanks_note ltx_role_thanks"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">†</sup><span class="ltx_note_type">thanks: </span><span id="id2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">hanyim@uchicago.edu</span></span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Quanjia Xiao
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Lei Pang
</span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Haixiao Liu
</span></span></div>
<div class="ltx_dates">August 24, 2026</div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose <span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FSPO</span> (Fair Sequence Policy Optimization), a sequence-level reinforcement learning method for LLMs that enforces length-fair clipping directly in the importance-sampling (IS) weight space. We revisit sequence-level RL methods and identify a mismatch when PPO/GRPO-style clipping is transplanted to sequences: a fixed clip range systematically reweights short vs. long responses, distorting the effective objective. Theoretically, we formalize length fairness via a Length Reweighting Error (LRE) and prove that small LRE yields a directional cosine guarantee between the clipped and true updates. FSPO introduces a simple, Gaussian-motivated remedy: we clip the sequence log-IS ratio with a band that applies a KL-corrected drift term and scales as <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. Empirically, FSPO flattens clip rates across length bins, stabilizes training, and outperforms all baselines across multiple evaluation datasets.</p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recent progress on reinforcement learning (RL) for large language models (LLMs) has been catalyzed by GRPO<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> and the broader RLVR<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite> paradigm, where rule-based, verifiable rewards are assigned to the <em id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">entire</em> response rather than token-wise signals. This framing proved effective for improving mathematical reasoning and other verifiable tasks. However, the optimization procedures used in early RLVR systems largely inherited token-level machinery from PPO-like methods<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>, including the use of token-level importance-sampling (IS) ratios and token-level clipping. Meanwhile, subsequent works began to emphasize that, once rewards are sequence-level, it is more faithful to operate with sequence-level IS and sequence-level clipping so as to match the reward granularity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>, <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Despite the shift toward sequence-level IS, the theoretical distinctions and practical consequences of clipping in the sequence-level IS setting remain under-explored. Most methods transplant the clipping mechanism from token-level methods directly: they exert a <em id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">fixed</em> clip range on the probability ratio of the whole sequence. We argue that directly using fixed clip ranges at sequence level is problematic: the drift and dispersion of sequence-level log ratios scale with response length <math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This paper studies sequence-level clipping through the lens of <em id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">length fairness</em>. We formalize a simple criterion: acceptance rates should be approximately constant across response lengths. We show that fixed sequence-level clipping violates this criterion and can distort the training target. To address this, we propose <span id="S1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FSPO</span> (Fair Sequence Policy Optimization). FSPO keeps the IS semantics intact and restores length fairness by using a KL-corrected and <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{L}</annotation></semantics></math>-scaled acceptance band on the sequence log-ratio, which equalizes acceptance across lengths.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">To ground our analysis, we evaluate <span id="S1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FSPO</span> on sequence-level RL for mathematical reasoning. We compare against two sequence-level baselines: (i) <em id="S1.p4.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">RLOO</em> with sequence-level IS and a fixed clip on the full-sequence ratio, and (ii) <em id="S1.p4.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">GSPO</em> sequence-level clipping with ratio normalization. We report Avg@32 on <span id="S1.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AMC23</span>, <span id="S1.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MATH500</span>, <span id="S1.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AIME24</span>, and <span id="S1.p4.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AIME25</span>, alongside diagnostic panels that measure acceptance-by-length to verify length fairness. Across two base model scales, we observe flatter acceptance across length bins, more stable training dynamics, and improved task scores; full results and ablations are presented in §<a href="#S4" title="4 Experimental Setup ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Paper structure.</span>
§<a href="#S2" title="2 Length Fairness and Length Reweighting Error (LRE) ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> motivates length fairness, formalizes length reweighting and its consequences, and explains why a <math id="S1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{L}</annotation></semantics></math> band achieves near-constant acceptance across lengths. §<a href="#S3" title="3 Method: FSPO ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> details FSPO and implementation notes, including diagnostics used throughout our experiments. We then present results and ablations, and conclude with future directions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Length Fairness and Length Reweighting Error (LRE)</h2>

<section id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Setup.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> be a context (prompt) drawn from a data distribution <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(s)</annotation></semantics></math>,
and let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="o\in\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o\in\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> be a response (a token sequence).
Under a policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">outcome distribution</em> is</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi_{\theta}}(o\mid s)\;=\;\prod_{t=1}^{L(o)}\pi_{\theta}\big(y_{t}\mid h_{t}(s,y_{&lt;t})\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi_{\theta}}(o\mid s)\;=\;\prod_{t=1}^{L(o)}\pi_{\theta}\big(y_{t}\mid h_{t}(s,y_{&lt;t})\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="o=y_{1:L(o)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">o=y_{1:L(o)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the decoder state (prefix-dependent sufficient state)
before emitting <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For a candidate policy <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, define the per-outcome log-importance ratio</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S(o\mid s)\;=\;\log\frac{P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(o\mid s)}{P_{\pi_{\theta}}(o\mid s)}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{L(o)}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S(o\mid s)\;=\;\log\frac{P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(o\mid s)}{P_{\pi_{\theta}}(o\mid s)}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{L(o)}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=\mathrm{len}(o)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>len</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=\mathrm{len}(o)</annotation></semantics></math> and fix a <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">length-indexed</em> band <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{L}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{L}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our acceptance event explicitly includes length:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{L}\;=\;\big\{\mathrm{len}(o)=L\ \ \text{and}\ \ |S(o\mid s)|\leq b_{L}\big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>len</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{L}\;=\;\big\{\mathrm{len}(o)=L\ \ \text{and}\ \ |S(o\mid s)|\leq b_{L}\big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We write expectations under the <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">target</em> law <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}</annotation></semantics></math> as
<math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\theta^{\prime}}[\cdot]\equiv\mathbb{E}_{s\sim p(s),\,o\sim P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(\cdot\mid s)}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\theta^{\prime}}[\cdot]\equiv\mathbb{E}_{s\sim p(s),\,o\sim P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(\cdot\mid s)}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math>,
and define</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q(L)\;=\;\mathbb{P}_{\theta^{\prime}}(A_{L}\mid L),\qquad g_{L}^{\star}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\theta^{\prime}}[\,G(o,s)\mid L\,],\qquad g_{L}^{b}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\theta^{\prime}}[\,G(o,s)\mid A_{L},\,L\,]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>G</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(L)\;=\;\mathbb{P}_{\theta^{\prime}}(A_{L}\mid L),\qquad g_{L}^{\star}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\theta^{\prime}}[\,G(o,s)\mid L\,],\qquad g_{L}^{b}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{\theta^{\prime}}[\,G(o,s)\mid A_{L},\,L\,],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">so that the unclipped target and its clipped surrogate are</p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{L}[\,g_{L}^{\star}\,],\qquad g^{(b)}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{L}[\,q(L)\,g_{L}^{b}\,]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{L}[\,g_{L}^{\star}\,],\qquad g^{(b)}\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{L}[\,q(L)\,g_{L}^{b}\,].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G(o,s)\triangleq A(o,s)\nabla_{\theta^{\prime}}\log P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(o|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G(o,s)\triangleq A(o,s)\nabla_{\theta^{\prime}}\log P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(o|s)</annotation></semantics></math> is the estimator standard policy gradient.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To measure <em id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">length fairness</em> we use:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Length Reweighting Error (LRE))<span id="S2.Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S2.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{q}=\mathbb{E}[q(L)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{q}=\mathbb{E}[q(L)]</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LRE}\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left|\frac{q(L)}{\bar{q}}-1\right|\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>LRE</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LRE}\;=\;\frac{1}{2}\,\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left|\frac{q(L)}{\bar{q}}-1\right|\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Small LRE means acceptance is nearly constant across lengths, so <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(b)}</annotation></semantics></math> does not reweight the length mixture.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We assume a mild within-length stability:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded Stratification)<span id="S2.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exists <math id="S2.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="S2.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S2.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\,g_{L}^{b}-g_{L}^{\star}\,\|\ \leq\ \eta\,\|g_{L}^{\star}\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\,g_{L}^{b}-g_{L}^{\star}\,\|\ \leq\ \eta\,\|g_{L}^{\star}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|g_{L}^{\star}\|]}{\|g^{\star}\|}\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\frac{\mathbb{E}[\|g_{L}^{\star}\|]}{\|g^{\star}\|}\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, which captures dispersion of per-length signal.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.1</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Directional guarantee under length fairness)<span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under <a href="#S2.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 2.1 (Bounded Stratification). ‣ Setup. ‣ 2 Length Fairness and Length Reweighting Error (LRE) ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\angle\!\big(g^{(b)},g^{\star}\big)\ \geq\ \frac{1-\rho}{1+\rho},\qquad\rho\ \leq\ \kappa\Big(\eta+(1+\eta)\,\mathrm{LRE}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.552em;" width="0.552em"><mi mathvariant="normal">∠</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>LRE</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\angle\!\big(g^{(b)},g^{\star}\big)\ \geq\ \frac{1-\rho}{1+\rho},\qquad\rho\ \leq\ \kappa\Big(\eta+(1+\eta)\,\mathrm{LRE}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of this Theorem can be found in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorems ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>. This theorem motivates the practice to enforce length-fairness in clipping mechanism, as it implies that smaller LRE provides a larger lower bound for the cosine similarity between the clipped gradient and true gradient.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2.2</span></span><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gaussian of sequence-level log ratio)<span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The sequence log-IS ratio admits an asymptotically Gaussian law:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{S_{L}-\mu_{L}}{\sqrt{L}}\ \Rightarrow\ \mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}),\qquad\mu_{L}=\Theta(L),\ \ \sigma^{2}&gt;0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{S_{L}-\mu_{L}}{\sqrt{L}}\ \Rightarrow\ \mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}),\qquad\mu_{L}=\Theta(L),\ \ \sigma^{2}&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">According to this theorem, choosing a band in log-IS space as <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\quad b_{L}=\mu_{L}+z\,\sigma\,\sqrt{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\quad b_{L}=\mu_{L}+z\,\sigma\,\sqrt{L}</annotation></semantics></math>
yields an acceptance <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(L)</annotation></semantics></math> that is approximately constant in <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> and preserves the length fairness required by Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Directional guarantee under length fairness). ‣ Setup. ‣ 2 Length Fairness and Length Reweighting Error (LRE) ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>. Proofs and precise assumptions (Markov additive-functional vs. LAN routes) are in Appendix <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix B Proof of Theorems ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Notice that</p>
<table id="S2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{L}=\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[S_{L}]=\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{L}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{L}=\mathbb{E}_{\theta}[S_{L}]=\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{L}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">And by linearity of expectation,</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{L}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}\right]=\sum_{t=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}\right]=\sum_{t=1}^{L}-\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}\left(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid h_{t})\ ||\ \pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot\mid h_{t})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>log</mi><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔻</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.667em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\sum_{t=1}^{L}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}\right]=\sum_{t=1}^{L}\mathbb{E}_{\theta}\left[\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{t}\mid h_{t})}\right]=\sum_{t=1}^{L}-\mathbb{D}_{\text{KL}}\left(\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid h_{t})\ ||\ \pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(\cdot\mid h_{t})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Thus, we can use an average of the negative KL-divergence between old and new policies times <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> as an approximation to <math id="S2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Method: FSPO</h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Objective</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each prompt <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> we sample <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> completions
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{y_{i}\}_{i=1}^{G}\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> and optimize</p>
<table id="S3.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{J}_{\text{FSPO}}(\theta^{\prime})\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{x,\{y_{i}\}}\!\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\text{min}\Big(\!\exp\!\big(S_{i}(\theta^{\prime})\big)\widehat{A}_{i}\ ,\exp\!\big(\mathrm{clip}\big(S_{i}(\theta^{\prime}),-b_{L_{i}},\,b_{L_{i}}\big)\big)\widehat{A}_{i}\Big)\;\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒥</mi><mtext>FSPO</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>G</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>G</mi></munderover><mrow><mtext>min</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>A</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{J}_{\text{FSPO}}(\theta^{\prime})\;=\;\mathbb{E}_{x,\{y_{i}\}}\!\left[\frac{1}{G}\sum_{i=1}^{G}\text{min}\Big(\!\exp\!\big(S_{i}(\theta^{\prime})\big)\widehat{A}_{i}\ ,\exp\!\big(\mathrm{clip}\big(S_{i}(\theta^{\prime}),-b_{L_{i}},\,b_{L_{i}}\big)\big)\widehat{A}_{i}\Big)\;\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the log-IS ratio is</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{i}(\theta^{\prime})\;=\;\log\frac{P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(y_{i}\mid x)}{P_{\pi_{\theta}}(y_{i}\mid x)}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{L_{i}}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{i}(\theta^{\prime})\;=\;\log\frac{P_{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}}(y_{i}\mid x)}{P_{\pi_{\theta}}(y_{i}\mid x)}\;=\;\sum_{t=1}^{L_{i}}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}=\mathrm{len}(y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>len</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}=\mathrm{len}(y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{i,t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{i,t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the decoder state for prefix <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y_{i,&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y_{i,&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The clip band is defined in <em id="S3.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">log-IS</em> space:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{L}\;=\;\underbrace{\hat{\mu}\,L}_{\text{drift}}\;+\;\underbrace{z\,\hat{\sigma}\,\sqrt{L}}_{\text{scale}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>drift</mtext></munder><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>scale</mtext></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{L}\;=\;\underbrace{\hat{\mu}\,L}_{\text{drift}}\;+\;\underbrace{z\,\hat{\sigma}\,\sqrt{L}}_{\text{scale}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">so
<math id="S3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\exp(\mathrm{clip}(S_{i},-b^{-}_{L_{i}},b^{+}_{L_{i}}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>b</mi><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\exp(\mathrm{clip}(S_{i},-b^{-}_{L_{i}},b^{+}_{L_{i}}))</annotation></semantics></math> is the sequence-level clipped ratio (IS weight).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Below are some implementation notes on FSPO.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Drift estimation.</span>
In practice we can estimate <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> by a running average of the observed forward KL:
On the <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-th minibatch <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{|B_{k}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{|B_{k}|}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{i}=\mathrm{len}(y_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>len</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{i}=\mathrm{len}(y_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{tok}}=\sum_{i=1}^{|B_{k}|}L_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>tok</mtext></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{tok}}=\sum_{i=1}^{|B_{k}|}L_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We compute the average KL statistic:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{KL}^{\text{token}}_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{N_{\text{tok}}}\sum_{i=1}^{|B_{k}|}\sum_{t=1}^{L_{i}}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>KL</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>token</mtext></msubsup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>tok</mtext></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>L</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{KL}^{\text{token}}_{k}\;=\;\frac{1}{N_{\text{tok}}}\sum_{i=1}^{|B_{k}|}\sum_{t=1}^{L_{i}}\log\frac{\pi_{\theta^{\prime}}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})}{\pi_{\theta}(y_{i,t}\mid h_{i,t})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Note that this is a common metric logged during training process and also is used to compute the KL-loss in previous works <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite> (KL-loss is not used in FSPO). We maintain an exponential moving average (EMA) to stabilize the computation:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{k}\;=\;(1-\alpha)\,\hat{\mu}_{k-1}\;+\;\alpha\,(-\mathrm{KL}^{\text{token}}_{k})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.170em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>KL</mi><mi>k</mi><mtext>token</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{k}\;=\;(1-\alpha)\,\hat{\mu}_{k-1}\;+\;\alpha\,(-\mathrm{KL}^{\text{token}}_{k}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is the current number of mini-batch, and set <math id="S3.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{L}=L\hat{\mu}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{L}=L\hat{\mu}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Scales.</span>
In the formula of the scale in <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> is used to control the desired clipfrac and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> can be estimated using a running average estimator similar to <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>.
In practice, to simplify implementation process and minimize engineering overhead, we manually set <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=z\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=z\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> as a single hyperparameter and tuned it. This also enables a fairer comparison with prior methods, most of which use heuristically chosen clip ranges. We ablate the effect of different <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> values in Appendix <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Ablations of Hyperparameters ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>. A natural extension is to set different scale parameter <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{upper}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{upper}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{lower}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{lower}</annotation></semantics></math>, which allows separate control of upper clip-range and lower clip-range as mentioned in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dual-clip</span>
We noticed that current implementations of RL methods generally include <em id="S3.SS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">dual-clip</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, effectively clipping the ratio by <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\epsilon_{c})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\epsilon_{c})</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In our experiments, we implement dual-clip also in log-space with <math id="S3.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>L</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{L}</annotation></semantics></math>-scaled clip range.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experimental Setup</h2>

<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Models and data.</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our method based on two base LLMs: <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen3-1.7B-Base</span> and <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Qwen3-8B-Base</span>.
For training, we use the <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">DAPO</span> dataset <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite> together with AIME problems up to and including 2023 (AIME<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math>23). Evaluation uses held-out math benchmarks including <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MATH500</span>, <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AMC23</span>, <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AIME24</span>, and <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">AIME25</span>. Unless otherwise stated, we report <span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Avg@32</span> (average per-sample accuracy with 32 sampled completions).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Training framework.</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We build on <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">VeRL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite> with vLLM and Megatron as backends. All models are trained under the same sampling policy, batch sizes, and total token budgets. Full hyperparameters and infra details are listed in Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Training Configurations ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.3 </span>Baselines.</h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare against sequence-level RL baselines: <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RLOO</span> (sequence-level IS with a fixed clip), <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GSPO</span> (normalized-ratio clipping), and our <span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FSPO</span>. We also include GRPO as an important baseline. All methods share identical data, sampling configurations, batch sizes, and training steps; FSPO only differs in the log-space clipping schedule.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Results</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Main results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 5.1 Main results ‣ 5 Results ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarizes Avg@32 across benchmarks and model sizes.
We observe FSPO is better on both sizes especially for 8B, and tends to produce flatter clip fractions and more stable training dynamics; detailed fairness diagnostics follow immediately below. (More evaluation results will be released soon).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="S5.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="S5.T1.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance across benchmarks. Avg@32: sampling 32 times. Cells show <span id="S5.T1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Avg@32</span>. Boldface indicates the best values.</span></figcaption>
<table id="S5.T1.6" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T1.6.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.6.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Method</span></th>
<td id="S5.T1.6.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">MATH500</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">AMC23</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">AIME24</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">AIME25</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Average</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.6.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.6.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"></th>
<td id="S5.T1.6.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Best/Last)</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Best/Last)</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Best/Last)</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Best/Last)</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.6.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">(Best/Last)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.6.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.6.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;" colspan="6"><span id="S5.T1.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Qwen3-1.7B-Base</span></th></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.6.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.6.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-left:7.0pt;padding-right:7.0pt;"><span id="S5.T1.6.4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">base</span></th>
