<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Preliminaries and Related Works</h2>

</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorems</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Directional guarantee under length fairness). ‣ Setup. ‣ 2 Length Fairness and Length Reweighting Error (LRE) ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h3>

<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cosine lemma.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For nonzero <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos\angle(u,v)\geq\frac{\|v\|-\|u-v\|}{\|v\|+\|u-v\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∠</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos\angle(u,v)\geq\frac{\|v\|-\|u-v\|}{\|v\|+\|u-v\|}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We also need another assumption.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Bounded co-variation)<span id="A2.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The residual co-variation between <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|q(L)-\bar{q}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|q(L)-\bar{q}|</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{L}^{\star}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{L}^{\star}\|</annotation></semantics></math> is mild so that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\big[\,|q(L)-\bar{q}|\,\|g_{L}^{\star}\|\,\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[|q(L)-\bar{q}|\big]\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[\|g_{L}^{\star}\|\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.500em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\big[\,|q(L)-\bar{q}|\,\|g_{L}^{\star}\|\,\big]\ \leq\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[|q(L)-\bar{q}|\big]\ \mathbb{E}\!\big[\|g_{L}^{\star}\|\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">This assumption is reasonable as we would not expect <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{L}^{\star}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{L}^{\star}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, i. e. the policy gradient at length <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>, to be larger when the clip ratio <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q(L)</annotation></semantics></math> deviates from average. Intuitively, they should be independent.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proof</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(b)}=\mathbb{E}_{L}[q(L)g_{L}^{b}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(b)}=\mathbb{E}_{L}[q(L)g_{L}^{b}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}=\mathbb{E}_{L}[g_{L}^{\star}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}=\mathbb{E}_{L}[g_{L}^{\star}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{q}=\mathbb{E}[q(L)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{q}=\mathbb{E}[q(L)]</annotation></semantics></math>.
Decompose</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{(b)}-\bar{q}\,g^{\star}=\mathbb{E}_{L}\big[(q(L)-\bar{q})\,g_{L}^{\star}\big]\;+\;\mathbb{E}_{L}\big[q(L)\,(g_{L}^{b}-g_{L}^{\star})\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.280em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mi>b</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{(b)}-\bar{q}\,g^{\star}=\mathbb{E}_{L}\big[(q(L)-\bar{q})\,g_{L}^{\star}\big]\;+\;\mathbb{E}_{L}\big[q(L)\,(g_{L}^{b}-g_{L}^{\star})\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By triangle inequality and <a href="#S2.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption 2.1 (Bounded Stratification). ‣ Setup. ‣ 2 Length Fairness and Length Reweighting Error (LRE) ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Assumption</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g^{(b)}-\bar{q}g^{\star}\|\leq\mathbb{E}\!\left[|q(L)-\bar{q}|\,\|g_{L}^{\star}\|\right]+(1+\mathrm{LRE})\,\bar{q}\,\eta\,\mathbb{E}\|g_{L}^{\star}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>LRE</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g^{(b)}-\bar{q}g^{\star}\|\leq\mathbb{E}\!\left[|q(L)-\bar{q}|\,\|g_{L}^{\star}\|\right]+(1+\mathrm{LRE})\,\bar{q}\,\eta\,\mathbb{E}\|g_{L}^{\star}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|q-\bar{q}|]=2\bar{q}\,\mathrm{LRE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>LRE</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|q-\bar{q}|]=2\bar{q}\,\mathrm{LRE}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|g_{L}^{\star}\|=\kappa\|g^{\star}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|g_{L}^{\star}\|=\kappa\|g^{\star}\|</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g^{(b)}-\bar{q}g^{\star}\|\leq\bar{q}\,\kappa\Big(\eta+(1+\eta)\mathrm{LRE}\Big)\,\|g^{\star}\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>LRE</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g^{(b)}-\bar{q}g^{\star}\|\leq\bar{q}\,\kappa\Big(\eta+(1+\eta)\mathrm{LRE}\Big)\,\|g^{\star}\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=\frac{\|g^{(b)}-\bar{q}g^{\star}\|}{\bar{q}\|g^{\star}\|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=\frac{\|g^{(b)}-\bar{q}g^{\star}\|}{\bar{q}\|g^{\star}\|}</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the cosine lemma with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u=g^{(b)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u=g^{(b)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\bar{q}g^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\bar{q}g^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Weighted<span id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.1" class="ltx_text">-</span>LRE variant (assumption-free).</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">If one wants to avoid any bounded co-variation concerns, define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LRE}_{w}=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left|\frac{q(L)}{\bar{q}}-1\right|\frac{\|g_{L}^{\star}\|}{\mathbb{E}\|g_{L}^{\star}\|}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LRE</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>g</mi><mi>L</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LRE}_{w}=\frac{1}{2}\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left|\frac{q(L)}{\bar{q}}-1\right|\frac{\|g_{L}^{\star}\|}{\mathbb{E}\|g_{L}^{\star}\|}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Then the same argument yields the bound with <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LRE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LRE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LRE}</annotation></semantics></math> replaced by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LRE}_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>LRE</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LRE}_{w}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2 (Gaussian of sequence-level log ratio). ‣ Setup. ‣ 2 Length Fairness and Length Reweighting Error (LRE) ‣ Clip Your Sequences Fairly: Enforcing Length Fairness for Sequence-Level RL" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></h3>

</section>
</section>
